{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794843133,"nonce":"tTM964EVytSu5BaYrRbtPuGwxgQ=","title":"hxn check --browser passes a program that ends in an uncaught exception","message":"Under Ash, `hxn check hl --wasm --threads --browser` prints `PASS` when the program in the web page throws and never finishes.\n\nReproducer: hxn-gpu-webgpu at 0.3.0's worker (before `GPUAgent.present`), with the 0.3.1 check, which reads a canvas frame back in a submission after the one that rendered it. The page prints:\n\n    WebGPU error: Destroyed texture [...] used in a submit.\n    [ash] uncaught exception: instance of haxe.ValueException\n    [ash]   at fun$623(hxn/Inbox.hx:209)\n    [ash]   at sys.thread.EventLoop.loop(...)\n\nThe `canvas:` line never appears, but the check reports `PASS: gpu_webgpu ran on hl --wasm --threads --browser` and exits 0. A driver's own CI therefore cannot catch a failure like this; hxn-gpu's browser workflow caught it only because it greps for each expected line.\n\nThe check should fail when the page reports an uncaught exception, or when the program does not reach its end. The browser runner should also be checked for hxcpp.","files":null}]}